    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> be the vertices of a triangle and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> be the mid-point of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>G</mi></math> divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>M</mi></math> in the ratio, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math> , then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8736;</mi><mi>G</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>A</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;being the origin) is equal to",
